% A name that is a function's is still free to name a predicate: at the
% start of a body literal, length followed by a comparator or an operator is
% a call, and followed by anything else an atom.  So length/1 is defined and
% read beside the calls that share its name.
length("ab").
length(S) :- word(S), length(S) > 3.
word("abc"). word("abcd"). word("abcdef").
short(S) :- length(S), length(S) + 0 < 3.

length(S)?
short(S)?
